	<h2>From the Escalation Queue to Platform Engineering</h2>
	<p>
		I am <strong>Keshav Bhardwaj</strong>, an enterprise support engineer with over 5 years of experience keeping mission-critical digital experiences and telecom backends running quietly in production.
	</p>
	<p>
		For the past <strong>3.5+ years at Acquia (Dec 2022 – Present)</strong>, I have served as a Drupal Digital Experience (DXP) Support Engineer. I own high-severity production escalations for global enterprise brands running on Acquia Cloud and Site Factory. My day-to-day work lives deep in PHP stack traces, database deadlocks, varnish caching topologies, and containerized platform infrastructure.
	</p>

	<h2>Early Foundations: Telecom Operations at Bharti Airtel</h2>
	<p>
		Before joining Acquia, I spent 18 months (June 2021 – Dec 2022) at <strong>Diksha Technologies catering to Bharti Airtel</strong> as an Application & Database Support / Operations Engineer. Operating in a 24x7 telecom environment taught me the gravity of 99.99% SLAs, how to troubleshoot Linux server performance under heavy load, and how to communicate clearly with leadership during major network incidents.
	</p>

	<h2>The DevOps & SRE Evolution</h2>
	<p>
		Supporting large-scale systems eventually leads to a fundamental realization: <em>the fastest way to resolve an outage is to prevent it by architecture</em>. 
	</p>
	<p>
		Over the past two years, I have actively expanded my engineering scope into modern Cloud and Platform engineering:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Containers & Orchestration:</strong> Packaging applications into minimal, secure Docker images and managing declarative deployments, Services, and Ingress routing in Kubernetes.</li>
		<li><strong>Cloud Infrastructure:</strong> Designing resilient compute, networking (VPCs, Subnets), and security policies across Amazon Web Services (AWS).</li>
		<li><strong>CI/CD Pipelines:</strong> Writing automated GitHub Actions workflows for continuous integration, linting, testing, and deployment.</li>
		<li><strong>Automation & Workflow Orchestration:</strong> Building automated diagnostic scripts in Python and event-driven alerting bridges with self-hosted n8n.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Leadership Philosophy</h2>
	<blockquote>
		"Every outage is a conversation between a distributed system and the people who rely on it."
	</blockquote>
	<p>
		When systems fail, blame solves nothing. The best engineers build runbooks, automate repetitive toil, and turn customer pain into measurable Service Level Objectives (SLOs). My goal as a technical leader is to build platforms and teams that fail gracefully, recover fast, and become a little more boring every quarter.
	</p>

	<p>
		I am always open to discussing DevOps opportunities, Kubernetes platform design, and site reliability engineering. Feel free to connect with me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/keshavbhardwaz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> or check out my work on <a href="https://github.com/keshavbhardwaz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
	</p>
